From eefd3b15af5777db5a370739d37ca7bcb3af8caa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 14:58:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03097/11362] [outer-loop] ARC gate: CORE set-containment
 verdict (fix the score-lever solve-rate guard)

Root cause of the A1/A2 score-lever failures: the gate's _verdict compared raw
solved-COUNT over a search whose CORE solves land at ~7724-7792 actions on an
8000 budget (97% of cap). A lever that merely REORDERS the chaotic near-budget
trajectory flips one knife-edge solve 4<->3 -> automatic FAIL regardless of
merit. A1 (no-op recall 0.053, prunes ~nothing) still dropped m0r0
7789->unsolved@7803; A2 same signature. Both positive_controls PASSED, proving
the METRIC was broken, not the levers.

Fix: _verdict now uses CORE set-containment. CORE = the games the baseline
solves {lp85,m0r0,sp80,vc33}. A lever must preserve EVERY core solve (set, not
count) and cut median actions on the FIXED core denominator; new fringe solves
are a reported BONUS, never netted against a core loss. This is the only
relaxation that still FAILs a config trading core solves for fringe (A2). Legacy
count fallback keeps it working against an old baseline JSON.

measure() now emits solved_games + actions_by_game (auto-persist on
--update-baseline). Four+ regression fixtures
(tests/python/test_arc_submission_gate_verdict.py) lock the property: A1->FAIL,
A2->FAIL, positive->PASS(IMPROVED), neutral->PASS(non-inferior), bonus reported,
legacy fallback. Verified on the REAL A1 artifact: control(baseline-vs-itself)
-> PASS non-inferior (old gate false-failed this); A1 with_prune -> FAIL lost
m0r0 (still caught).

Protects the conductor's queued .417 A3/A4/A6 from false-failing the same way
(B2 canonicalizes this gate but lands AFTER A3/A4/A6 in roadmap order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
